1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,838
Hi, this is GridMind AI, built for the MongoDB Harness Engineering and Model Wrangling hackathon.

2
00:00:05,838 --> 00:00:17,213
GridMind is a multi-agent harness that analyzes a real electrical grid, fixes it, proves the fix, and remembers what worked, with MongoDB Atlas as its memory and its single source of truth.

3
00:00:18,113 --> 00:00:22,747
AI data centers are adding megawatts to grids that were built for homes and shops.

4
00:00:22,747 --> 00:00:29,811
Our demo network is the public CIGRE medium voltage benchmark, with a four megawatt AI data center connected at bus fourteen.

5
00:00:29,811 --> 00:00:33,258
The overview shows what the solver found at the evening peak:

6
00:00:33,258 --> 00:00:34,445
seventeen violations.

7
00:00:34,445 --> 00:00:41,961
Fourteen buses are below the voltage limit, the lowest at zero point eight nine five per unit, and three transformers are overloaded.

8
00:00:41,961 --> 00:00:46,369
Every number on every page is read from a power flow result stored in MongoDB.

9
00:00:47,269 --> 00:00:49,053
This is the heart of the app:

10
00:00:49,053 --> 00:00:53,852
the complete single line diagram, generated from the circuit model in MongoDB.

11
00:00:53,852 --> 00:01:01,419
Every bus, line, transformer, load and data center device is drawn, and each violation is colored exactly where it happens.

12
00:01:01,419 --> 00:01:03,696
Orange is a violation, red is severe.

13
00:01:03,696 --> 00:01:10,894
Ten layers switch the view between voltage, loading, current, active and reactive power, losses, and the data center.

14
00:01:11,794 --> 00:01:14,428
Click any component to see everything about it.

15
00:01:14,428 --> 00:01:19,809
Here is bus eleven, at zero point nine two three per unit, or eighteen point four six kilovolts.

16
00:01:19,809 --> 00:01:29,673
Every parameter is tagged as source input or assumption, and the panel shows the diagnosed cause, the supply path from the grid, and its history across every stored simulation.

17
00:01:30,573 --> 00:01:34,311
Pressing Run starts ten specialized agents in a dependency graph.

18
00:01:34,311 --> 00:01:37,935
Circuit modeling, power flow and violation detection run first.

19
00:01:37,935 --> 00:01:41,443
Root cause, data center and memory retrieval run in parallel.

20
00:01:41,443 --> 00:01:48,748
Then corrective action, optimization and independent verification repeat in a bounded loop until the network is proven healthy.

21
00:01:48,748 --> 00:01:55,707
Every task and the full run state are written to MongoDB after each step, so a run survives a restart and can be resumed.

22
00:01:56,607 --> 00:01:59,365
The root cause agent explains why, with numbers.

23
00:01:59,365 --> 00:02:09,303
It splits the voltage drop along every supply path into its resistive and reactive parts, checks transformer tap headroom, and solves the grid again without the data center.

24
00:02:09,303 --> 00:02:11,774
Feeder one fails because of line impedance.

25
00:02:11,774 --> 00:02:15,278
The data center buses fail because of the data center itself.

26
00:02:16,178 --> 00:02:23,222
The corrective action agent generates nineteen remedies that match those causes, and sizes each one by simulation:

27
00:02:23,222 --> 00:02:32,492
capacitor banks from a measured voltage sensitivity, tap positions from a full sweep, transformer upgrades, tie switches, and data center flexibility.

28
00:02:32,492 --> 00:02:38,238
The ranked plans compare voltage, loading, losses, cost and residual violations side by side.

29
00:02:39,138 --> 00:02:44,342
The optimizer evaluated one hundred seventy nine plans, each with real AC power flows.

30
00:02:44,342 --> 00:02:48,215
Its proposal, drawn in purple, costs sixty two thousand dollars:

31
00:02:48,215 --> 00:02:59,409
a fifteen hundred kilovar capacitor bank, three tap steps on one transformer, shifting a third of a megawatt of AI training out of the evening peak, and discharging the on-site battery.

32
00:03:00,309 --> 00:03:01,887
Then governance takes over.

33
00:03:01,887 --> 00:03:05,629
The independent verification agent does not trust the optimizer.

34
00:03:05,629 --> 00:03:10,365
It reloads the model from MongoDB and solves it again, at peak and at light load.

35
00:03:10,365 --> 00:03:13,464
Only then does the app label the circuit as verified.

36
00:03:13,464 --> 00:03:14,809
Zero violations remain.

37
00:03:15,709 --> 00:03:18,888
The before and after page proves it in the same layout:

38
00:03:18,888 --> 00:03:21,490
seventeen resolved, zero remaining, zero new.

39
00:03:21,490 --> 00:03:29,410
Minimum voltage rises from zero point eight nine five to zero point nine five three per unit, and network losses drop by about a quarter.

40
00:03:30,310 --> 00:03:34,285
The data center is part of the same network, not a separate dashboard.

41
00:03:34,285 --> 00:03:43,426
Cooling follows real weather from Open Meteo, homes and businesses follow public SimBench load profiles, and a twenty four hour AC time series checks every hour.

42
00:03:43,426 --> 00:03:49,445
A linear program then moves flexible AI training to cheaper hours without breaking a single network limit.

43
00:03:50,345 --> 00:03:52,366
This is the memory of the harness.

44
00:03:52,366 --> 00:03:56,884
After verification, the learning agent stores structured lessons in MongoDB:

45
00:03:56,884 --> 00:04:01,104
which remedy worked, for which violation, with its measured parameters.

46
00:04:01,104 --> 00:04:09,545
When we ran a second scenario, an AI training surge, the agents retrieved those lessons, tried the proven plan first, and were verified again.

47
00:04:09,545 --> 00:04:11,625
The system improves with every run.

48
00:04:12,525 --> 00:04:14,400
We are explicit about our claims.

49
00:04:14,400 --> 00:04:21,216
The objective function is shown in full, and the result is called the best of the evaluated plans, not a proven optimum.

50
00:04:21,216 --> 00:04:24,284
The language model never calculates electrical values.

51
00:04:24,284 --> 00:04:26,669
It only explains evidence from the solver.

52
00:04:27,569 --> 00:04:33,841
Finally, the report agent writes a complete engineering report from the stored results, ready to download and share.

53
00:04:34,741 --> 00:04:40,142
GridMind AI is a persistent, self-improving and governed agent harness on MongoDB Atlas.

54
00:04:40,142 --> 00:04:44,008
It turns a failing grid into a verified plan in about a minute.

55
00:04:44,008 --> 00:04:49,102
The code is on GitHub at github dot com, slash Azii Darvii, slash gridmind dash ai.

56
00:04:49,102 --> 00:04:49,715
Thank you.
